# rote — example environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in only the variables you need.
# All variables below are optional — `rote` auto-detects which
# graduator driver to use based on what's installed and what's set
# in your environment.
#
#   Driver priority (auto-detect):
#     1. claude  — Claude Code CLI + subscription auth  (no env var needed)
#     2. codex   — Codex CLI + ChatGPT subscription     (no env var needed)
#     3. api     — Anthropic SDK + API key              (requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)
#
# Override the auto-detect with `rote graduate --agent <name>`.
#
# See docs/agent-runtime.md for the full driver design.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `api` driver — Anthropic SDK with API-key auth
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Only needed if you want to use `rote graduate --agent api` (runs
# the graduator in-process via the `anthropic` Python SDK). Requires
# `pip install rote-cli[api]`.
#
# Users with a Claude Max/Pro subscription should prefer the
# `claude` driver — it uses your subscription and needs no API key.
# ClaudeDriver deliberately scrubs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from the
# subprocess env to force subscription auth, so setting this var
# does NOT affect the claude driver.

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-...

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `claude` driver — Claude Code subscription via OAuth token
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Optional long-lived OAuth token for Claude Code, for CI environments
# where interactive `claude login` hasn't been run. See:
# https://code.claude.com/docs/en/authentication
#
# When set, `claude -p` in print mode uses this token instead of
# the interactive login. Useful for containerized or headless runs.

# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-...

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `codex` driver — ChatGPT subscription
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# No env var needed. The Codex CLI reuses the cached login from
# `~/.codex/auth.json` (created by running `codex login` once).
# rote's CodexDriver does not scrub OPENAI_API_KEY, so if you have
# it set in your environment AND an active ChatGPT login, codex
# will use the subscription (the ChatGPT login wins by default).
